<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Select Triangles Based on Edge Length</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select &gt; Scan Data &gt; Based On Edge Length</b></span>.</p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Select Triangles Based On Edge Length</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command selects visible triangles based on the length of their sides. There are upper and lower limits for the distance between adjacent points and adjacent stripes.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_triangles_edge.gif" width="266px" height="605px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Maximum distance between points on the same stripe</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">This option specifies the maximum distance ModelMaker will allow between points within a stripe. Click the checkbox to apply the operation, and enter the distance in mm in the text box.</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Default value</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">is 2mm.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Minimum distance between points on the same stripe</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">This option specifies the minimum distance ModelMaker will allow between points within a stripe. Click the checkbox to apply the operation, and enter the distance in mm in the text box.</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Default value</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">is 0.001mm.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Maximum distance between stripes</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">This option specifies the maximum distance ModelMaker will allow between stripes. Large gaps appear between stripes when scanning too fast. Scanning too rapidly results in large spaces between stripes, which would result in a poor scan, missing large areas of detail for example. Click the checkbox to apply the operation, and enter the distance in mm in the text box.</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Default value</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">is 5mm.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Minimum distance between stripes</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">This option specifies the minimum distance ModelMaker will allow between stripes. Large gaps appear between stripes when scanning too fast. Scanning too rapidly results in large spaces between stripes, which would result in a poor scan, missing large areas of detail for example. Click the checkbox to apply the operation, and enter the distance in mm in the text box.</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Default value</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">is 0.001mm.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP937472067" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table class="TableGrid" style="margin-left:23.4pt; border-collapse:collapse; border-spacing:0px;" cellspacing="0">
<tr>
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image322.gif" width="200px" height="149px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs7">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB">In this example, a surface with a large overhang is scanned.</span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image323.gif" width="200px" height="149px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs7">
<p class="Normal" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB">Point A and Point B will be joined in the resulting patch, missing a significant area of detail.</span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image324.gif" width="200px" height="149px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs7">
<p class="Normal" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB">A top down view of the resulting patch shows that large triangles have been created.</span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image325.gif" width="200px" height="149px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs7">
<p class="Normal" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB">If the object is scanned again from another angle, it will create confusing, inaccurate data because of the large triangles. The data from the second scan will not match the existing data.</span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image326.gif" width="200px" height="149px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs7">
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-GB">In <i>System &gt; Hardware</i> dialog (Scanning tab) we can specify the maximum distance ModelMaker will allow between points within a stripe and between stripes within a patch, preventing the problem above.</span></p>
<p class="whs8"><span lang="EN-GB">See</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB">Hardware Settings - Scanning</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">for details.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="margin-left:19px;">&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command works on scan data only. Note that it removes any previous scan data selections. Other data types remain unaffected.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for different distances</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP225986631" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table class="TableGrid" style="border-collapse:collapse; border-spacing:5px;" cellspacing="5">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs9">
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image331.jpg" width="292px" height="174px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image333.jpg" width="291px" height="174px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs9">
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:center;" align="center"><span lang="EN-GB">Distance between selected points is from 0.4 to 0.6mm</span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:center;" align="center"><span lang="EN-GB">Distance between selected stripes is from 0.5 to 1.5mm</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for real selection of <span lang="EN-GB" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Triangles Based On Edge Length</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP938112441" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_edge_length.gif" width="332px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p class="Use"><span class="Command">Select Triangles Based On Edge Length</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>useful</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">if you want to select data produced by poor scanning technique. If the sensor is moved too quickly when scanning, the distance between stripes may be large giving poor quality data. Similarly if the sensor is moved very slowly then the stripes will be very close together. Other problems may occur where points on a stripe are far apart, for example when scanning a vertical step.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="javascript:void(0);" onclick="var e; if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion)&gt;=4){e=event;} if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion) &gt;=2 &amp;&amp; typeof(PopupMenu_Invoke) == 'function') PopupMenu_Invoke(e,'','Select by Point Normal','Select_by_Point_Normal.htm','Select Reverse Scans','Select_Reverse_Scans.htm','Select Thin Triangles','Select_Thin_Triangles.htm','Select Triangles Based on Order','Select_Triangles_Based_on_Order.htm');return false;" title=""><img src="../images/ss_btn_see_also.gif" border="0" height="17" width="60" alt=""></a></span></p>

